.TH YOUCAM 1 "November 2026" "youcam 1.0-beta1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
youcam \- floating camera overlay and screen recorder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B youcam
.RB [ \-\-smoke\-test ]
.RB [ \-\-record\-test
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-snapshot
.IR dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B youcam
shows the camera in a floating window without a frame (a circle, square or
rectangle) that stays above other windows, and records the screen with the
camera and the microphone.
Drag the camera to move it and scroll on it to resize it.
Right\-click it (or Control\-click) for every control: camera, microphone,
shape, recording area, transparency, Center Stage, background, recording
format and the recording panel.
.PP
Movies are saved to the Desktop as
.IR YouCam\-Recording\-<date>\-<time>.mov
(or the chosen recording format).
Running
.B youcam
again while it is open brings back a hidden camera.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Start, open the camera and quit after a few seconds; for checks.
.TP
.BI \-\-record\-test " seconds"
Make a real recording of that length without dialogs, save it and quit.
.TP
.BI \-\-snapshot " dir"
Render the windows to PNG files in
.I dir
and quit.
.SH GLOBAL SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Control\-Alt\-Super\-R
Start or stop recording.
.TP
.B Control\-Alt\-Super\-P
Pause or resume recording.
.PP
They go through the GlobalShortcuts portal; GNOME asks to confirm them once.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YOUCAM_ENCODER
.BR va ,
.B nvenc
or
.BR x264 :
force a video encoder instead of the first one available in that order.
.TP
.B YOUCAM_CAPTURE
.B portal
or
.BR mutter :
force the ScreenCast portal or Mutter's screen cast for recording.
.TP
.B YOUCAM_CONFIG
Use this preferences file instead of the default one.
.TP
.B YOUCAM_SNAPSHOT_PROJECT
With
.BR \-\-snapshot ,
a project
.I .youcam.mkv
whose Choose After Recording window is also rendered.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/youcam/prefs.ini
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/youcam/room\-*.png
The empty room learned for each camera (Background \(-> Learn Empty Room).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/youcam/pending/
Recordings kept for Choose After Recording.
.SH NOTES
On GNOME the
.B YouCam Capture Exclusion
Shell extension keeps the recording panel and area guides out of the
recording. Log out and in once after installing, then run
.BR "gnome\-extensions enable youcam\-capture\-exclusion@youcam.app" .
The tray icon needs the AppIndicator extension on GNOME.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome\-extensions (1)
.PP
https://github.com/antirez/youcam
